# Ignore file for web/Dockerfile specifically (BuildKit reads
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to a root `.dockerignore`).
#
# It lives here rather than at the repo root so that this card touches nothing
# outside `web/`: the agent-worker image is a separate service with a different
# context, and a single shared root ignore file would be one file two cards edit.
# If a builder ever ignores this in favour of a root file, the only consequence
# is a larger context and a slower build, never a wrong image.
#
# The build context is the REPO ROOT, because the app reads `../data` at request
# time - so `data/` is deliberately not excluded here.
#
# Env files: never. Mirrors the root `.dockerignore`: the env contract is
# `agent/.env.example` and the real values are Railway service variables. This
# file needs its own copy of the rule because `web/Dockerfile` does `COPY web ./`
# into the builder stage, and `next build` reads `.env.local` - so a developer's
# local env file would be both copied into a layer and baked into the build.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
# The agent tree is not part of the web image. Its own service builds it.
agent
# Agent scratch space and per-agent worktrees: never part of any service image.
hive
worktrees
